==Strategy==
Although there are some powerful [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies at the beginning, they can easily be stalled if you have all [[Treasure#Unstarred Alien stats decrease|anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]]. '''''Only''''' bring dedicated [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien cats]] if they actually prove to be difficult, as you want all the firepower you can get for the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies. Since the main threats don't spawn until the Aliens are defeated, try to lure the second wave of Scissoroos in front of the [[Cat Base]] so you can build up an army before facing the Dark enemies.

The combined DPS of the Shadow Boxer Ks and Gory Darks will rip through even the tankiest of cats. In fact, almost every heavy attacker will only get to kill a few of the Boxers/Gories before dying, especially slower ones like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] and [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togelan Pasalan]]. If you have to use one, choose a fast attacker such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]].

Since most heavy attackers are just wasted slots, focus on cheaper ones with [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Waves]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surges]] and quick attack speed, like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]] ([[True Form]] recommended), [[Catway (Super Rare Cat)|Drone Cat]] and [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Sexy Legs Cat]]. Using a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] will allow you to spam them more easily.

No matter what, do not use any form of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]], [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]], any [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan]] [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cat]] [[Li'l Titan Cat (Special Cat)|variant]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] nor anybody else with short range or Single Attack (with a few exceptions). While all the enemies are outranged by Awakened Bahamut Cat, their pushing power is so high that he ends up being near-useless unless you can keep the enemies frozen.

If you have [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], use him. As long as you can keep them alive, the Dark enemies' threat level will be next to none once you have two unsynced Bombercats on the screen.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that attacks fast and/or is [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] should do well, but below this will have more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage. Note that most, if not all [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] do not do well here, as the Dark enemies' DPS are absurdly high. Obviously, any [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusive will make this stage a breeze.
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Kenshin]]: Her powerful [[Knockback]] ability is able to keep many of the Dark enemies at bay here, as well as doing some good damage to them from range.
*[[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars, Type Φ]]: Does [[Massive Damage|Masive Damage]] to Aliens and Darks. Multi-Hit can juggle most Darks around, dramatically reducing their pushing power.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: His Normal Form is a spammable attacker that will melt the Darks in this stage within seconds.
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bora]]: If you are having trouble killing the Alien enemies before the Dark enemies appear, Bora will make that a lot easier, but is generally not recommended for the Dark enemies' phase.
*[[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Shingen]]: An Attacks Only unit that can hurt both traits in the stage. If protected well, his 120K+ damage at level 30 can reduce them to rubble.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]]: Her fast, hard-hitting, piercing [[Long Distance]] attack makes her usage similar to Twinstars in this stage, just without the massive damage ability.
*[[Ryu (Uber Rare Cat)|Ryu]]: A fast-attacking generalist, his range allows him to pierce the Dark enemies' defenses easily, along with his [[Savage Blow|Savage Blows]].

