==Trivia==
*''Gestalt'' is a word meaning "something greater than the sum of its parts".
*Gestalt, Decay is a reference to the psychological phenomenon [[wikipedia:Gestaltzerfall|Gestaltzerfall]], also known as Gestalt decomposition. When one is exposed to words or character patterns for a prolonged period of time, it may appear to them that the shapes are decomposing or "decaying" into their constituting parts.
*Gestalt, Decay and the Japanese names of [[Body & Soul]] (心と体、繋ぐもの ''Kokoro to Karada, Tsunagu Mono'', "Mind and Body, That Which Connects") and [[At Least I'm a Cat]] (せめて、ネコらしく ''Semete, Nekorashiku'', "At Least, Be a Cat") follow a similar format to most ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' episode titles - note the commas. This may be because Body & Soul and [[Weak & Mildly Acidic]] are the 27th and 28th [[Stories of Legend]] sub-chapters, and ''Neon Genesis Evangelion'' has 26 episodes in the series plus two in ''[https://wiki.evageeks.org/The_End_of_Evangelion End of Evangelion]''.

